# --- Secrets: nothing below this line may ever be committed ---
# Deliberately broad. `.env.*` only matches a DOT separator, so .env-sample,
# .env_prod and .envrc all slipped through it. `.env*` catches every variant;
# the template is the single explicit exception.
.env*
!.env.example
.env.github.actions

# Google service-account keys. The job reads the JSON from an env var, so a key
# file should never be in the tree at all -- these patterns are a safety net.
*-service-account*.json
service-account*.json
gcp-*.json
credentials.json
*.pem

# Working copy of the Google Form answers. The submitted version lives in
# docs/self-review.md; this one is formatted for pasting box by box.
FORM-ANSWERS.md

# --- Private working documents (not part of the submission) ---
# The job ad, the technical challenge brief, and my internal build plan.
# This repo is shared with the reviewer; these do not belong in it.
ad.md
AI Systems Engineer Technical.md
Campaign_Tracker_Build_Brief.md

